  "worked_solution": "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \nWith that in mind, let's examine our statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n12u-18v=2(6u-9v).\n$$\n\nSince $u$ and $v$ are integers, $6u-9v$ must be an integer, too. So, $2∣(12u-18v).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n12u-18v=6(2u-3v).\n$$\n\nSince $u$ and $v$ are integers, $2u-3v$ must be an integer, too. So, $6∣(12u-18v).$\n\n- Statement III is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n12u-18v=3(4u-6v).\n$$\n\nSince $u$ and $v$ are integers, $4u-6v$ must be an integer, too. So, $3∣(12u-18v).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
